{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% block body %}
    <div class="container nt-faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>

        <h5 class="mt-4">How do I use these trackers?</h5>
        <p>Copy your list from the <a href="/list">List</a> page and paste it into your torrent client, or give your client the API link
            shown there so it stays up to date. To add them to a single download, paste its magnet link or .torrent into
            <a href="/tools">Tools</a>.</p>

        <h5 class="mt-4">Which trackers are best?</h5>
        <p>See <a href="/rankings">Rankings</a>: the most reliable over the last two weeks, the longest unbroken uptime, and the
            fastest from each region.</p>

        <h5 class="mt-4">I submitted a tracker but it wasn't added. Why?</h5>
        <p>The <a href="/submitted">Submitted</a> page shows the reason for every attempt. The usual ones:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>It's the same server as a tracker already listed (only one is kept, preferring UDP, then HTTP, then HTTPS).</li>
            <li>It wasn't answering when it was tried.</li>
            <li>It only accepts certain torrents (private or whitelisted trackers can't be tested).</li>
            <li>Its hostname points to a private or local address.</li>
            <li>It was removed in the last 30 days for being down or unreliable.</li>
            <li>Its owner opted out with a <a href="https://www.bittorrent.org/beps/bep_0034.html">BEP34</a> DNS record.</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="mt-4">A tracker works for me but shows as Down or Up/Bad. Why?</h5>
        <p>It's tested from several countries, and must hand out real peers and no fake ones. See <a href="/about">About</a> for what each status means,
            and <a href="/fix">How to fix a tracker</a> if it's yours.</p>

        <h5 class="mt-4">How is the score worked out?</h5>
        <p>Availability &times; stability over recent days, with penalties for failed tests and very slow replies. Details on the
            <a href="/about">About</a> page.</p>

        <h5 class="mt-4">I run a tracker.</h5>
        <p>Its own page (the <i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line" style="color:#c15cff"></i> icon) shows what the checks saw; if
            something's wrong, <a href="/fix">How to fix</a> explains it, and <b>Check again now</b> re-tests once you've fixed it.
            On that page you can also <b>Follow</b> its status changes (Atom feed) and copy a status badge for your site (offered while it's healthy); the same
            data is at <code>/api/tracker/&lt;host&gt;</code>.</p>
        <p>To set its protocol and port, or to opt out, publish a <a href="https://www.bittorrent.org/beps/bep_0034.html">BEP34</a>
            DNS record. For anything else, use the email link at the bottom of the page.</p>

        <h5 class="mt-4">Where's the code? How do I report a bug?</h5>
        <p>On <a href="https://github.com/KolanTheKoala/newtrackon-nz">GitHub</a>; report problems as
            <a href="https://github.com/KolanTheKoala/newtrackon-nz/issues">issues</a>.</p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
{% set title = "FAQ - newTrackon" %}
